# At 25 C the NTC is 10 kohm, matching r1, so A0 sits at half of the Nano's 5V pin (~2.38 V on USB)
# and the LED stays off. At 40 C the NTC drops to 5.330 kohm (Vishay NTCLE100E3103JB0 p10 table),
# pulling A0 to 65.23 % of 5V (~3.10 V) and lighting the LED; the sketch's B = 3977 K conversion
# prints 39.7 C. At 10 C it rises to 19.872 kohm (~1.60 V, sketch prints 10.4 C), off again.
open
step 100ms
expect @nano.A0 > 2.25V
expect @nano.A0 < 2.50V
expect @led1 off
expect serial contains "temp=25.0 C"
set temperature 40
step --until @led1 lit --timeout 150ms
step 50ms
expect @nano.A0 > 3.00V
expect @nano.A0 < 3.25V
expect @led1 lit
expect serial contains "temp=39.7 C"
set temperature 10
step --until @led1 off --timeout 150ms
step 50ms
expect @nano.A0 > 1.45V
expect @nano.A0 < 1.70V
expect @led1 off
expect serial contains "temp=10.4 C"
expect no diagnostics
